# Commits that only moved text around, and that `git blame` should look straight
# through to whoever actually wrote each line.
#
# HOW TO USE IT
#
# Git does not read this file on its own. Turn it on once, per clone:
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# GitHub reads it automatically, with no configuration at all.
#
# WHAT BELONGS IN IT
#
# Only commits that changed no behaviour whatsoever -- a formatter run, a
# whitespace sweep. Never a rename, a refactor, or "mostly formatting". The file
# is only useful while every entry in it is certainly harmless, because a reader
# who finds one exception stops trusting the whole list and blames through it by
# hand anyway.

